---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';

const chapters = [
  { id: 'the-spark', label: 'The spark' },
  { id: 'karting', label: 'A family effort' },
  { id: 'breakthrough', label: 'Finding my pace' },
  { id: 'cars', label: 'The move to cars' },
  { id: 'endurance', label: 'Running the team' },
  { id: 'electric', label: 'An electric first' },
  { id: 'paddock', label: 'Beyond the cockpit' },
];
---

<Base title="Motorsport" description="Drew Cleaver's motorsport story: a family trip to IMSA in 1995, junior karting, endurance racing, and an electric time-attack win." compact noindex>
  <article class="motorsport-story" aria-labelledby="motorsport-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <header class="story-hero">
        <div class="story-kicker"><p class="eyebrow">Drew Cleaver · Motorsport</p><span>Since 1995</span></div>
        <h1 id="motorsport-title" class="serif">It started with<br /><em>a radio call.</em></h1>
        <div class="hero-bottom">
          <p class="story-deck">My dad won race tickets on a radio talk show. That family outing became karting weekends, a shared ambition, and a life that keeps finding its way back to the track.</p>
          <a class="story-start" href="#the-spark">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Chapters in my motorsport story">
        <p class="eyebrow">The road here</p>
        <ol>
          {chapters.map(({ id, label }, index) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}><span aria-hidden="true">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>{label}</a></li>)}
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <section class="story-chapter" id="the-spark" aria-labelledby="spark-title">
        <div class="chapter-meta"><span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><p>1995</p><p>Texas World Speedway</p></div>
        <div class="chapter-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">The spark</p>
          <h2 id="spark-title" class="serif">Free tickets.<br />A lasting obsession.</h2>
          <p>In 1995, my dad called into a radio talk show and won tickets to the IMSA race at Texas World Speedway. We went as a family. That's where this story begins.</p>
          <p>A call to a radio show had put us at a sports car race. The next chapter would put my brother Matt and me behind the wheel ourselves.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="story-chapter" id="karting" aria-labelledby="karting-title">
        <div class="chapter-meta"><span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><p>The karting years</p><p>Katy, Texas → SKUSA Red River</p></div>
        <div class="chapter-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">A family effort</p>
          <h2 id="karting-title" class="serif">Two brothers.<br />One used Margay.</h2>
          <p>We started at GCKI in Katy, sharing a used Margay chassis with a 100cc Yamaha KT100. Eventually, one shared kart became two Gold chassis, and we each had a seat of our own.</p>
          <p>Then Matt made a decision that changed my racing. My older brother stopped driving to focus on helping me succeed. When I moved into 80cc Junior, the effort behind my seat became even more of a family project.</p>
          <p>I raced a CRG chassis that Ryan Briscoe had used at the Charlotte CIK race. Kawasaki sponsorship came when I was 11, turning 12—the minimum age—midseason. With 80cc Junior came travel, as we took on the SKUSA Red River regional tour.</p>
          <aside class="story-aside" aria-label="A family turning point">
            <p>Matt stepped out of his seat to help me make more of mine.</p>
            <span>That belongs in the story as much as any result.</span>
          </aside>
          <p>Racing introduced me early to the people who make an individual result possible. The driver gets the name on the timing sheet; the work is shared.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="story-chapter" id="breakthrough" aria-labelledby="breakthrough-title">
        <div class="chapter-meta"><span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><p>2001</p><p>Texas karting</p></div>
        <div class="chapter-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Finding my pace</p>
          <h2 id="breakthrough-title" class="serif">A newspaper feature.<br />A Grand Prix win.</h2>
          <p>Around May 2001, I was featured in the <em>Houston Chronicle</em>. That September, I won the Texas Superkart Grand Prix. Those are two landmarks I still connect with that chapter of my life.</p>
          <p>Support during my karting years included Kawasaki, Royal Purple, Bieffe Helmets, Aerografix helmet painting, NAPA Auto Parts, and a private investment firm. Alongside my family, those supporters helped make the racing possible.</p>
          <p>My introduction to sponsorship came from being the young driver receiving that support. Years later, I'd get to experience the relationship from the other side.</p>
          <div class="chapter-record"><span>September 2001</span><strong>Texas Superkart Grand Prix winner</strong></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="story-interlude">
      <div class="shell interlude-inner"><p class="eyebrow">Karts gave me the start.</p><p class="serif">Cars opened up<br /><em>the possibilities.</em></p><span>Autocross · Track days · Time trials · Endurance</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="shell">
      <section class="story-chapter" id="cars" aria-labelledby="cars-title">
        <div class="chapter-meta"><span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><p>The move to cars</p><p>Cones, road courses & the drag strip</p></div>
        <div class="chapter-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Finding more ways to drive</p>
          <h2 id="cars-title" class="serif">If there was a way<br />to drive it, I was interested.</h2>
          <p>At 15, I entered a Mazda Rev It Up autocross using someone else's credentials, before I was old enough to enter myself. It's one of the less polished details of the story. There was also SCCA autocross, entered properly under my own name, and drag racing at Houston Raceway Park.</p>
          <p>In 2005, I was doing track days in my dad's 2005 BMW E46 M3 Competition. Driving the Texas Motor Speedway roval at night is another memory that belongs in this chapter.</p>
          <p>NASA Time Trials in a Panoz GTWC added another kind of experience. Across karting, autocross, drag racing, track days, and time trials, I kept coming back to the same fascination: understanding a car, finding its limits, and learning how to drive it better.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="story-chapter" id="endurance" aria-labelledby="endurance-title">
        <div class="chapter-meta"><span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">05</span><p>Endurance racing</p><p>Lemons · ChampCar · WRL</p></div>
        <div class="chapter-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Running the team</p>
          <h2 id="endurance-title" class="serif">The whole operation<br />has to finish.</h2>
          <p>Eventually, racing meant running our own amateur endurance sports car team. We raced in the 24 Hours of Lemons, ChampCar, and World Racing League. A WRL win became part of that story, too.</p>
          <p>Endurance racing expands what it means to do well. A fast lap is one piece. Preparation, reliability, pit work, driver changes, communication, and judgment all become part of the same result.</p>
          <p>That is the connection I see between racing and operating a business. You have to understand the whole effort, decide what matters next, and work with the people around you. The habit began with a shared kart and grew into responsibility for a team.</p>
          <div class="chapter-record"><span>World Racing League</span><strong>Race-winning endurance experience</strong></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="story-chapter electric-chapter" id="electric" aria-labelledby="electric-title">
        <div class="chapter-meta"><span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">06</span><p>2020</p><p>Pikes Peak International Raceway<br />Colorado</p></div>
        <div class="chapter-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">An electric first</p>
          <h2 id="electric-title" class="serif">Same clock.<br /><em>Different powertrain.</em></h2>
          <p>At PPIR in Colorado in 2020, I won Street Class in GRIDLIFE Time Attack in an EV, competing against combustion-powered cars. It was the first EV win against internal-combustion cars in GRIDLIFE Time Attack history.</p>
          <p>For me, that result connects the racing driver with the inventor: curiosity about a different way of doing something, followed by a real test. The stopwatch makes the comparison concrete.</p>
          <div class="chapter-record"><span>2020 · GRIDLIFE · PPIR</span><strong>Street Class winner · Electric vehicle</strong></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="story-chapter" id="paddock" aria-labelledby="paddock-title">
        <div class="chapter-meta"><span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">07</span><p>The wider paddock</p><p>Daytona & Circuit of the Americas</p></div>
        <div class="chapter-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Beyond the cockpit</p>
          <h2 id="paddock-title" class="serif">Driver. Operator.<br />Sponsor. Guest.</h2>
          <p>My connection to motorsport also includes NASCAR Truck Series sponsorship at Circuit of the Americas, and being a TRG hospitality guest at the Daytona 24 Hours and with its GT3 entry at COTA.</p>
          <p>Those experiences added the sponsor and guest perspective to the one I already knew as a driver and team operator. The racing matters, and so does how people experience the weekend: how they're welcomed, what they connect with, and what makes them want to return.</p>
          <p>That's where my interests meet today—racing, business, and hospitality. I'm interested in what happens on track and in the work that makes the experience around it possible.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <footer class="story-close">
        <p class="eyebrow">Still finding my way back to the track</p>
        <h2 class="serif">Have a racing story<br /><em>of your own?</em></h2>
        <p>If we shared a paddock, a grid, or one of these weekends, I'd love to hear from you. And if you're working on something in motorsport, let's talk.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/contact/">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={profile.bookingUrl}>Schedule a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        <a class="back-to-top" href="#motorsport-title">Back to the start <span aria-hidden="true">↑</span></a>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Each chapter is a self-contained flow: future real figures can sit inside
     .chapter-copy or span its grid without reserving empty media space now. */
  .motorsport-story { --copper: #995827; }
  .story-hero { padding-block: 2rem 2.5rem; }
  .story-kicker { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap: .5rem 1rem; align-items: baseline; }
  .story-kicker > span { font: .75rem/1.6 ui-monospace, monospace; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .story-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 8.5vw, 6.8rem); margin: 2rem 0 1.8rem; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.055em; }
  .story-hero h1 em { color: var(--copper); }
  .hero-bottom { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.4rem 3rem; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; }
  .story-deck { max-width: 43rem; font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.3rem); line-height: 1.7; }
  .story-start { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.8rem; min-height: 44px; font-size: .875rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--copper); }
  .chapter-nav { border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding-block: 1.25rem; }
  .chapter-nav ol { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: .15rem 1.5rem; margin-top: .6rem; }
  .chapter-nav a { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .8rem; min-height: 44px; font-size: .875rem; }
  .chapter-nav a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .chapter-nav a span { color: var(--copper); font: .75rem/1.5 ui-monospace, monospace; }
  .story-chapter { display: grid; gap: 1.6rem; padding-block: 3rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .chapter-meta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr); gap: .15rem 1rem; align-content: start; font: .75rem/1.65 ui-monospace, monospace; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .chapter-number { grid-row: span 2; color: var(--copper); font: 2.6rem/1 var(--serif); letter-spacing: -.05em; }
  .chapter-copy { min-width: 0; max-width: 42rem; }
  .chapter-copy > .eyebrow { color: var(--copper); }
  .chapter-copy h2 { margin: .7rem 0 1.5rem; font-size: clamp(2.15rem, 4.8vw, 3.45rem); line-height: 1.12; }
  .chapter-copy > p:not(.eyebrow) { margin-top: 1.1rem; font-size: 1.025rem; line-height: 1.85; }
  .story-aside { border-left: 2px solid var(--copper); padding: .3rem 0 .3rem 1.3rem; margin-block: 2rem; }
  .story-aside p { font: 1.65rem/1.35 var(--serif); letter-spacing: -.025em; max-width: 26rem; }
  .story-aside span { display: block; font-size: .8125rem; color: var(--color-muted); margin-top: .8rem; }
  .chapter-record { display: grid; gap: .35rem; margin-top: 1.7rem; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; background: #e9ece1; border-left: 2px solid #9baa8a; }
  .chapter-record span { font: .7rem/1.6 ui-monospace, monospace; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; }
  .chapter-record strong { font-size: .9375rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .story-interlude { background: var(--green); color: var(--paper); }
  .interlude-inner { padding-block: 3rem; }
  .interlude-inner > .serif { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 5rem); line-height: 1.1; margin: 1rem 0 1.4rem; }
  .interlude-inner > span { display: block; color: #d5dfce; font-size: .8125rem; }
  .electric-chapter h2 em { color: var(--copper); }
  .story-close { padding-block: 3rem; max-width: 46rem; }
  .story-close h2 { font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.4rem); margin: 1rem 0 1.4rem; }
  .story-close > p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 38rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .back-to-top { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .7rem; min-height: 44px; margin-top: 2rem; text-decoration: underline; font-size: .8125rem; }
  @media (min-width: 560px) { .chapter-nav ol { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  @media (min-width: 800px) {
    .story-hero { padding-block: 3.5rem 3rem; }
    .story-hero h1 { margin-block: 2.5rem 2rem; }
    .chapter-nav { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 150px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 3rem; align-items: baseline; }
    .chapter-nav ol { margin-top: 0; }
    .story-chapter { grid-template-columns: 150px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 3rem; padding-block: 4.5rem; }
    .chapter-meta { display: block; padding-top: .2rem; }
    .chapter-number { display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 3.5rem; }
    .chapter-meta p + p { margin-top: .6rem; }
    .interlude-inner { padding-block: 4.5rem; padding-left: 198px; }
    .story-close { margin-left: 198px; padding-block: 4.5rem; }
  }
</style>
